# il-snapshot.py --compare (plan 5.12.4) is the proof that a milestone leaves
# the IL and diagnostics of 'clang -S' and llc byte-identical (D14 frozen,
# 5.10.13: M15 gate step 19; the M18, M19 and M20 gates too). A gate only
# compares snapshots that should be equal, so a comparison that looked at the
# file names or sizes alone, or skipped the .err files, would pass every gate.
# Inputs/il-snapshot/il-snapshot-selftest.py loads the script as a module and
# runs compare() on copies of the fixture snapshot Inputs/il-snapshot/baseline
# made under %t: equal trees, and trees that differ only in il-snapshot.json,
# give 0; a changed .il (one byte, same size), a changed .err (its exit
# status), an .il with CRLF line endings, a file only in the old tree and
# files only in the new one give a nonzero result and list each file as
# 'differs: <name>', 'missing: <name> (only in <old>)' or
# 'extra: <name> (only in <new>)'. It also checks that main() exits 2,
# naming the problem and creating no --out, on usage errors: --compare
# naming a missing directory, --out inside --compare, --out inside the
# repository or holding it (%t lies in the repository with the usual build
# directory, so the selftest names repository paths itself), no PATH,
# --jobs 0. The input list (only files HEAD tracks, minus each --exclude; a
# directory excludes its subtree) is checked through tracked_inputs() with
# the module's git() replaced by a fake 'ls-tree -r -z --name-only HEAD'
# listing: a file exclude removes that file and a directory exclude its
# subtree (each with the number of inputs it removed), msil/test/M1/00 does
# not exclude msil/test/M1/00-smoke, an exclude that matches nothing counts
# 0, tracked files that are not .c or .ll are no inputs, overlapping paths
# give each input once, the list is sorted, and git is asked for HEAD once
# per path; find_inputs() prints 'note: --exclude <path> matches no input'
# for exactly the excludes that removed nothing. Nothing runs git, clang or
# llc. M18's --normalize forms (5.12.4, M18 gate step 14: on both sides short
# branches become long ones, 'ldc.i4.m1', 'ldc.i4.<n>' and 'ldc.i4.s <n>'
# become 'ldc.i4 <n>' and ' nomangle cdecl' becomes ' cdecl') is checked on
# an old and a new copy of the fixture: an .il whose copies differ only in
# those forms, in both directions, gives 0, lists nothing and prints
# '--normalize forms: ... 1 of them differ only in those forms' (without
# --normalize the same trees differ); with a branch label changed as well it
# is listed and diffed between the normalized texts, while another .il that
# differs only in a form is counted, not listed; the same kinds of change in
# an .err file are listed (only .il files are normalized); --normalize
# without --compare exits 2 and creates no --out. M20's --skip-changed
# (5.12.4) is checked on a new copy that lacks the four files of a skipped
# input and has a changed .err of another: compare() leaves the skipped
# files out, counts them ('--skip-changed: 4 files of 1 inputs changed
# against HEAD were not compared') and still lists the .err, and
# changed_inputs() asks a fake git for 'status --porcelain -z
# --untracked-files=all -- <paths>' once and takes a modified file, an
# untracked one and both names of a rename; --llc-arg is checked on the
# commands Snapshot.compile() builds (nothing runs): llc gets each argument,
# clang '-mllvm <argument>'.

# RUN: rm -rf %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/il-snapshot/il-snapshot-selftest.py %S/../../utils/il-snapshot.py %t > %t.log
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t.log "^ok: compare equal$" "^ok: compare stamp-only$" "^ok: compare changed-il$" "^ok: compare changed-err$" "^ok: compare changed-eol$" "^ok: compare missing$" "^ok: compare extra$" "^ok: compare mixed$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t.log "^ok: usage compare-not-a-directory$" "^ok: usage out-inside-compare$" "^ok: usage out-inside-repository$" "^ok: usage out-holds-repository$" "^ok: usage no-path$" "^ok: usage jobs-zero$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t.log "^ok: exclude file$" "^ok: exclude directory$" "^ok: exclude boundary$" "^ok: exclude no-match$" "^ok: exclude non-input$" "^ok: exclude duplicates$" "^ok: exclude sorted$" "^ok: exclude note$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t.log "^ok: compare normalize-forms$" "^ok: compare normalize-real-difference$" "^ok: compare normalize-err-exact$" "^ok: usage normalize-without-compare$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t.log "^ok: compare skip-changed$" "^ok: skip-changed git-status$" "^ok: llc-arg commands$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} lacks %t.log "^FAIL"
